## Version

`hono@4.12.23`

## What is the expected behavior?

A `/**` wildcard route should match regardless of what other routes are registered on the same app.

## What is the actual behavior?

A `/**` wildcard route returns 404 when `SmartRouter` falls back from `RegExpRouter` to `TrieRouter` (e.g., when overlapping parameterized segments exist).

## Minimal reproduction

```ts
import { Hono } from 'hono';

const app = new Hono();
app.all('/auth/**', (c) => c.text('auth'));
app.get('/pkg/:name/:version', (c) => c.text('pkg'));
app.get('/pkg/:name/versions', (c) => c.text('versions'));

const r1 = await app.fetch(new Request('http://localhost/auth/test'));
const r2 = await app.fetch(new Request('http://localhost/pkg/lodash/1.0'));
const r3 = await app.fetch(new Request('http://localhost/pkg/lodash/versions'));

console.log('/auth/test:', r1.status);      // 404 ← BUG (expected 200)
console.log('/pkg/lodash/1.0:', r2.status);  // 200
console.log('/pkg/lodash/versions:', r3.status); // 200
```

## Root Cause

Two issues in `TrieRouter`'s handling of `**`:

1. **`getPattern('**')` returns `null`** (`src/utils/url.ts`) — only `'*'` is recognized as a wildcard, so `**` is treated as a literal path segment
2. **`node.insert()` stores the child under key `'**'`** (`src/router/trie-router/node.ts`) — but `search()` looks up `children['*']`, so the wildcard node is never found

Most apps don't hit this because `SmartRouter` defaults to `RegExpRouter` (which handles `**`). The bug surfaces when `RegExpRouter` can't handle the route set (overlapping param segments like `/:name/:version` + `/:name/versions`) and falls back to `TrieRouter`.

**Direct reproduction on TrieRouter:**
```ts
import { Hono } from 'hono';
import { TrieRouter } from 'hono/router/trie-router';

const app = new Hono({ router: new TrieRouter() });
app.all('/auth/**', (c) => c.text('auth'));
app.get('/other', (c) => c.text('other'));

await app.fetch(new Request('http://localhost/auth/test'));   // 404 ← always fails
await app.fetch(new Request('http://localhost/other'));       // 200
```

## Fix

PR: #4977 — two-line fix:
- `getPattern()`: recognize `'**'` as equivalent to `'*'`
- `node.insert()`: use `'*'` as the child key when pattern is a wildcard

## Workarounds

- Use `/*` instead of `/**`

## 🐛 Bug Report

**Severity:** High  
**Category:** Error Handling  
**Location:** `src/compose.ts` (lines 50-58), `src/hono-base.ts` (lines 358-361)

**Found by:** [WhiteRose](https://github.com/shakecodeslikecray/whiterose) - AI-powered bug hunter  
**Bug ID:** WR-001

---

## 📋 Description

The middleware composition in Hono only handles exceptions that are instances of the `Error` class. If a middleware throws a value that is **not** an `Error` (e.g., a string, number, or plain object), the error handling mechanism bypasses custom `onError` handlers and leads to an **unhandled promise rejection**, potentially crashing the application.

---

## 🔍 Vulnerable Code Path

**Step 1:** Middleware throws non-Error value
```typescript
// src/compose.ts:52
res = await handler(context, () => dispatch(i + 1))
// Middleware throws: throw "something went wrong"
```

**Step 2:** Caught but not wrapped
```typescript
// src/compose.ts:54
if (err instanceof Error && onError) {
  // This fails for non-Error values!
}
```

**Step 3:** Re-thrown without handling
```typescript
// src/compose.ts:57
throw err  // Non-Error value propagates
```

**Step 4:** Same issue in hono-base.ts
```typescript
// src/hono-base.ts:358
if (err instanceof Error) {
  // Also fails for non-Error values
}
// Line 361
throw err  // Unhandled promise rejection!
```

---

## 💥 Impact

- **Bypasses custom error handlers:** User-defined `onError` handlers are never called
- **Application crashes:** Unhandled promise rejections can crash the process
- **Poor error visibility:** Errors don't get logged or handled properly

---

## ✅ Suggested Fix

Wrap non-Error values in an `Error` object before processing:

**In `src/compose.ts`:**
```typescript
} catch (err) {
  const error = err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(String(err))
  if (onError) {
    await onError(error, context)
    // ...
  }
}
```

**In `src/hono-base.ts` (#handleError method):**
```typescript
#handleError(err: unknown, c: Context<E>) {
  const error = err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(String(err))
  // Use 'error' instead of 'err' for rest of method
}
```

---

## 🧪 Reproduction

```typescript
import { Hono } from 'hono'

const app = new Hono()

app.use('*', async (c, next) => {
  throw "This is not an Error object!"  // ❌ Causes unhandled rejection
})

app.onError((err, c) => {
  console.log('This never gets called!')
  return c.text('Error handled', 500)
})

export default app
```

**Expected:** `onError` handler catches the error  
**Actual:** Unhandled promise rejection, app crashes

---

## 🔗 References

- **WhiteRose:** https://github.com/shakecodeslikecray/whiterose
- **Detection Pass:** error-propagation-trace
- **Related:** This affects both `compose.ts` and `hono-base.ts`

---

💡 **Community contribution welcome!** This is a great first issue for contributors familiar with error handling.

